#: ../../source/json5_README.md:138
msgid ""
"Parses a JSON5 string, constructing the JavaScript value or object "
"described by the string. An optional reviver function can be provided to "
"perform a transformation on the resulting object before it is returned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/json5_README.md:142 ../../source/json5_README.md:158
msgid "Syntax"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/json5_README.md:145 ../../source/json5_README.md:162
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/json5_README.md:146
msgid "`text`: The string to parse as JSON5."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/json5_README.md:147
msgid ""
"`reviver`: If a function, this prescribes how the value originally "
"produced by parsing is transformed, before being returned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/json5_README.md:150 ../../source/json5_README.md:183
msgid "Return value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/json5_README.md:151
msgid "The object corresponding to the given JSON5 text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/json5_README.md:153
msgid "JSON5.stringify()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/json5_README.md:154
msgid ""
"Converts a JavaScript value to a JSON5 string, optionally replacing "
"values if a replacer function is specified, or optionally including only "
"the specified properties if a replacer array is specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/json5_README.md:163
msgid "`value`: The value to convert to a JSON5 string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/json5_README.md:164
msgid ""
"`replacer`: A function that alters the behavior of the stringification "
"process, or an array of String and Number objects that serve as a "
"whitelist for selecting/filtering the properties of the value object to "
"be included in the JSON5 string. If this value is null or not provided, "
"all properties of the object are included in the resulting JSON5 string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/json5_README.md:169
msgid ""
"`space`: A String or Number object that's used to insert white space into"
" the output JSON5 string for readability purposes. If this is a Number, "
"it indicates the number of space characters to use as white space; this "
"number is capped at 10 (if it is greater, the value is just 10). Values "
"less than 1 indicate that no space should be used. If this is a String, "
"the string (or the first 10 characters of the string, if it's longer than"
" that) is used as white space. If this parameter is not provided (or is "
"null), no white space is used. If white space is used, trailing commas "
"will be used in objects and arrays."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/json5_README.md:177
msgid "`options`: An object with the following properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/json5_README.md:178
msgid "`replacer`: Same as the `replacer` parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/json5_README.md:179
msgid "`space`: Same as the `space` parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/json5_README.md:180
msgid ""
"`quote`: A String representing the quote character to use when "
"serializing strings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/json5_README.md:184
msgid "A JSON5 string representing the value."
msgstr ""

